{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792493765,"nonce":"+Mr2RgObJzmJIcSc4Ta361AyEwA=","message":"Committed as 0d9f2bc03b710641ac030e52671c26692fa15628.\n\nThe interpreter and native backends now share value size, alignment and tagged/C-union payload offsets. Size/alignment queries do not allocate field-offset vectors. Constructors use declared variant discriminants and initialize unused storage; payloads include nested struct padding and can exceed the old fixed buffer.\n\nUnion parameters travel by address and direct union returns use caller-owned destinations. LLVM entry promotion accepts matching supported layouts. Address-taken union-returning functions remain excluded because their callers cannot supply the destination. Unsupported native storage shapes retain explicit errors.\n\nInterpreter bytecode supports construction, tag reads and payload extraction. Aggregate loads/extractions and returns retain independent values. Cranelift stages union phi inputs before committing their storage; LLVM carries union phis as values, so a later loop iteration cannot overwrite an earlier value's bytes. Small native copies are inline; larger ones use bounded memory intrinsics.\n\nRegression coverage includes integer tag widths, non-index discriminants, C unions, empty variants, 24-byte and 136-byte aggregate payloads, two independent returns, loaded copies, loop-carried values and swapping phis, and mixed Cranelift/LLVM callers and callees. Native compilation is asserted before executing code.\n\nThis is shared compiler groundwork. TypeScript scalar-union lowering is not enabled by this commit, and its four KNOWN_FAILURES entries are unchanged. Reference-bearing variants still need ownership/drop validation before frontend support; indirect union-return ABI and SIMD payload layouts remain separate work. No performance measurement is claimed.\n\nFinal validation: all ten union tests pass with LLVM, including the default LLVM engine and the interpreter/native bridge. The bridge first executes with unpublished native entries, then publishes the constructor and echo signatures separately and asserts native-entry hits. Seven union tests passed without LLVM before adding that bridge test. The LLVM compiler regression run passed 39 tests (including the then-eight union cases), plus five ABI unit tests and thirteen interpreter unit tests. TypeScript passed all 31 Rust tests with default features and again with LLVM. The live pinned TypeScript 6.0.2/Node comparison across interpreter, baseline and LLVM profiles remains 462 PASS / 12 XFAIL, with no unexpected failures. Compiler library/new-test Clippy with warnings denied, formatting and staged whitespace checks pass. Reports and logs are under /private/tmp/union-*.","files":null}]}